      ],
      "reasoning": "The authors state that the TMS factor structure was heterogeneous and then selectively report only the subscale that appeared more stable. The Curiosity subscale is also not cleanly separated from Decentering in either group, so the selection does not establish that Curiosity is a valid, distinct construct. The instructions were modified without the modification being reported, so it is unclear whether the scale measures the same construct in both groups. Together these issues weaken confidence that the Curiosity result reflects the intended construct. The authors should report the modified instructions in full and test measurement invariance or justify the Curiosity-only analysis as exploratory."
