          "observation": "Table 2 shows MTotal correlated with Watching (.613**), Touching (.593**), Repetitive Sounds (.344**), Simulations (.289**) and Mouth Sounds (.254**). MTotal is the average of the 14 items that make up these factors, so these correlations are part-whole and not independent evidence. The table has about 30 correlations, none corrected for multiplicity."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "MTotal is defined from the same items as the five factor scores, so its correlations with those factors are inflated by construction and cannot be read as separate effects. The text nonetheless attributes the TMS-Curiosity effect to the Touching and Repetitive Sounds factors (lines 271-272) and the marginal MAAS effect to Simulations (lines 275-276), each with p values near .04 to .008. With roughly 30 uncorrected tests, these isolated findings are fragile. This affects the claims about which triggers relate to curiosity and the interpretation of the cognitive-process account in the Discussion."
